{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/931494-storium","id":931494,"title":"Storium","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T11:45:09-07:00","id":931494,"title":"Storium","content":"So I just found out about this and it honestly seems really cool: <a href=\"https://storium.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://storium.com/</a><br /> <br /> It's basically a website that facilitates play-by-post RPG campaigns with narrative cards and minimal rules as a framework. I haven't got a chance to play with it yet, but as someone who really struggles to get a standard campaign together ot seems like a godsend. There's generic settings available for free and a paid membership program to get the original settings, which I normally wouldn't care about except it has Robin Laws' &quot;The Esoterrorists&quot; and something called &quot;Squatchtown&quot; from Wraith's Rich Dansky out right now, and Kenneth Hite's &quot;The Day After Ragnarok&quot; and the awesome old In Nomine settings coming later.<br /> <br /> Anyone here used it, or back the Kickstarter? Would there be interest in a possible campaign of something using it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T08:54:43-07:00","id":937114,"title":"","content":"Played it a bit and came to the conclusion that it is a great game...if you are a pro author or are really good at writing fiction. In the end, I felt I had to quit because my writing levels just weren't on the same plane as most of the others there. They sometimes wanted pages and pages of riveting dialogue and descriptions and perhaps for the first time since I started rping, I felt like I was just holding everyone back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T09:40:23-07:00","id":937148,"title":"","content":"I backed it, yes. I've never known anyone who was interested (and I invted people). Maybe, but I also have pretty severe avoidance... personality disorder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:36:03-07:00","id":937166,"title":"","content":"I ran a short game with it. I liked it, but it needs a more linear GMing style than I usually do, because the Narrator calls scenes and defines them in terms of challenges. It made it kinda hard to run the traditional investigation plot I tried. But I think if I'd had more time to adapt my style, it would've worked very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T16:37:43-07:00","id":937368,"title":"","content":"I happily backed it, and I agree with most of the above. I'm not sure how they could implement it, but it could really use some sort of better &quot;matching&quot; system than just the classifieds approach; and maybe a bit more support for different styles of being the Narrator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}